```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to flag something important before Morgan records the decision. Yesterday, while testing an unrelated replay tool, I measured a launch-period burst of about 18,000 events per minute. The hourly batch design cannot process that load within the customer-facing latency target. The streaming design can handle it, but it needs exactly 12 partitions for that load. I haven't updated the architecture document yet because the replay test was outside the launch checklist, but this directly impacts the architecture decision we're about to make."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you both for these critical flags. Ravi, the burst load finding is decisive — if the hourly batch design can't meet the customer-facing latency target at 18,000 events per minute, that architecture is disqualified for this launch. The streaming architecture with exactly 12 partitions is what we need. Leah, the compliance requirements are equally binding — EU data residency and a precise 400-day retention policy must be enforced regardless of architecture choice. Given that streaming is our only viable option for the load requirement, we need to confirm that the streaming architecture can also satisfy the EU residency and 400-day retention requirements. Can either of you — or anyone else on the call — confirm whether the streaming architecture as proposed supports EU-only data residency and configurable retention to exactly 400 days? If so, I'm prepared to settle on streaming with 12 partitions, EU residency, and 400-day retention. If there's any gap on the compliance side for streaming, we need to surface it now."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Morgan, I can speak to the load and partitioning side with confidence — the streaming architecture with exactly 12 partitions will handle the 18,000 events per minute burst within the latency target. However, I have to be straightforward: the EU data residency and 400-day retention requirements are outside what I've personally verified. I haven't tested or confirmed whether the streaming architecture as proposed supports EU-only data residency or configurable retention to exactly 400 days. That's something Leah or someone else on the compliance and infrastructure side would need to confirm before you record the decision. I don't want to guess on a binding compliance requirement two weeks before launch."}
